/* pocket4 — TWO-ROW waybar layout for a NARROW screen.

   Used whenever one row does not fit: portrait (either scale), and tablet mode
   in EITHER orientation. pocket4-waybar owns that rule; see its `layout_for`.
   The file used to be config-portrait.jsonc, chosen on orientation alone —
   tablet-mode landscape kept the one-row layout and lost ~240px of right-hand
   modules off the edge of the screen.

   Waybar renders a TOP-LEVEL ARRAY as multiple bars, so this file is an array
   of two bar objects rather than one object. Both include the shared module
   definitions from modules.jsonc — the definitions are NOT duplicated here.

   === THE WIDTH BUDGET IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THIS SPLIT ===

   The worst case is portrait + tablet mode: the panel is 1600 physical px
   across, which at scale 2.0 is 800 LOGICAL px — the narrowest surface this
   machine ever presents. Every module has a MINIMUM width it cannot compress
   below (CSS
   min-width, icon sizes, padding), and if a row's minimum exceeds the screen
   waybar commits a buffer wider than the surface Hyprland configured. Hyprland
   then squeezes that buffer into the visible box, so the bar renders
   HORIZONTALLY COMPRESSED **and taps land on the wrong module** — what you see
   at x is really the button at x * (buffer / screen). That is the bug this
   split exists to prevent; it is not cosmetic.

   Measured minimums at the time of writing (logical px, `hyprctl layers`):

     archicon 44   clock ~0*   sysinfo 85   workspaces 404 (469 with the
     scratchpad pill)   brightness 46   volume 75   tray 117   apps 56
     rotate 51   tabletmode 46   thermal 46   osk 46   display 59
     idle_inhibitor 41   language 41
     dictation: 126 idle, ~292 recording (REC + cleanup + cancel)

   * the clock's label ellipsizes, so it contributes ~0 to the MINIMUM even
     though it draws ~150px. Shrinkable modules are free here; fixed ones are not.

   Totals for the split below, at 800px: row 1 = 719, row 2 = 631 idle / 733
   recording. Both fit. The whole set is 1548 against 1600 (two rows), so there
   is very little room — check the arithmetic before adding a module here.

   KNOWN LIMIT, measured and deliberately not solved (2026-08-15). At 800px,
   opening one of ROW 1's drawers still exceeds the screen for as long as it is
   open, so the squeeze comes back while it is:

     row 1 collapsed          686   ok
     row 1 + sysinfo drawer   962   over by 162
     row 1 + backlight slider 860   over by 60
     row 1 + volume slider    850   over by 50

   Row 2's drawers are fine (648 with the display drawer open, against 476
   collapsed) — it has the slack, row 1 does not. No arrangement fixes it:
   expanding sysinfo costs +276 for its four readouts, and neither row has that
   much spare while holding everything else. Closing it would mean a materially
   smaller slider or fewer readouts, which is a call to make deliberately rather
   than by quietly shrinking things. */
[
  {
    /* Named so style.css can target this bar specifically — waybar adds `name`
       as a CSS class on the window, i.e. `window#waybar.narrow-top`. That is
       what lets the narrow layout shrink a module without affecting the one-row
       landscape bar or ideapad. */
    "name": "narrow-top",
    "layer": "top",
    "position": "top",
    "autohide": false,
    "autohide-blocked": false,
    "exclusive": true,
    "passthrough": false,
    "gtk-layer-shell": true,
    /* ROW 1 — what you GLANCE at: the clock, the readouts, and where you are. */
    "modules-left": [
      "custom/archicon",
      "clock",
      "group/sysinfo"
    ],
    "modules-center": [
      "group/workspaces"
    ],
    "modules-right": [
      "group/brightness",
      "group/volume"
    ],
    "include": ["{{ home }}/.config/waybar/modules.jsonc"]
  },
  {
    "name": "narrow-bottom",
    "layer": "top",
    "position": "top",
    "autohide": false,
    "autohide-blocked": false,
    "exclusive": true,
    "passthrough": false,
    "gtk-layer-shell": true,
    /* ROW 2 — what you PRESS. Voxtype's controls grow into this row's empty
       space while recording, so the workspace strip never shifts under a tap. */
    "modules-left": [
      "group/apps",
      "custom/voxtype-start",
      "custom/voxtype",
      "custom/voxtype-cleanup",
      "custom/voxtype-cancel",
      "custom/recording"
    ],
    "modules-center": [],
    "modules-right": [
      "custom/rotate",
      "custom/tabletmode",
      "custom/thermal",
      "custom/osk",
      "group/display",
      "network",
      "idle_inhibitor",
      "hyprland/language",
      "group/tray"
    ],
    "include": ["{{ home }}/.config/waybar/modules.jsonc"]
  }
]
